{"code":"27-1027.00","title":"Set and Exhibit Designers","description":"Design special exhibits and sets for film, video, television, and theater productions. May study scripts, confer with directors, and conduct research to determine appropriate architectural styles.","jobZone":5,"kinds":{"R":{"score":3.7,"share":0.1554},"I":{"score":2.75,"share":0.1007},"A":{"score":6.69,"share":0.3274},"S":{"score":3.04,"share":0.1174},"E":{"score":3.93,"share":0.1686},"C":{"score":3.27,"share":0.1306}},"highPoints":["A"],"tasks":[{"id":9289,"text":"Develop set designs, based on evaluation of scripts, budgets, research information, and available locations.","core":true,"importance":4.86,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.86},{"id":9286,"text":"Prepare rough drafts and scale working drawings of sets, including floor plans, scenery, and properties to be constructed.","core":true,"importance":4.8,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.65},{"id":9294,"text":"Prepare preliminary renderings of proposed exhibits, including detailed construction, layout, and material specifications, and diagrams relating to aspects such as special effects or lighting.","core":true,"importance":4.76,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.43},{"id":9305,"text":"Read scripts to determine location, set, and design requirements.","core":true,"importance":4.76,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.43},{"id":9293,"text":"Submit plans for approval, and adapt plans to serve intended purposes, or to conform to budget or fabrication restrictions.","core":true,"importance":4.62,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.38},{"id":9306,"text":"Attend rehearsals and production meetings to obtain and share information related to sets.","core":true,"importance":4.57,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.71},{"id":9287,"text":"Confer with clients and staff to gather information about exhibit space, proposed themes and content, timelines, budgets, materials, or promotion requirements.","core":true,"importance":4.52,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.48},{"id":9297,"text":"Research architectural and stylistic elements appropriate to the time period to be depicted, consulting experts for information, as necessary.","core":true,"importance":4.43,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.48},{"id":9303,"text":"Observe sets during rehearsals in order to ensure that set elements do not interfere with performance aspects such as cast movement and camera angles.","core":true,"importance":4.39,"relevance":95,"frequency":3.26},{"id":9296,"text":"Collaborate with those in charge of lighting and sound so that those production aspects can be coordinated with set designs or exhibit layouts.","core":true,"importance":4.33,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.4},{"id":9300,"text":"Select set props, such as furniture, pictures, lamps, and rugs.","core":true,"importance":4.16,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.4},{"id":9304,"text":"Design and build scale models of set designs, or miniature sets used in filming backgrounds or special effects.","core":true,"importance":4.05,"relevance":100,"frequency":2.76},{"id":9284,"text":"Examine objects to be included in exhibits to plan where and how to display them.","core":true,"importance":3.84,"relevance":95,"frequency":2.89},{"id":9302,"text":"Assign staff to complete design ideas and prepare sketches, illustrations, and detailed drawings of sets, or graphics and animation.","core":true,"importance":3.79,"relevance":95.24,"frequency":3},{"id":9290,"text":"Direct and coordinate construction, erection, or decoration activities to ensure that sets or exhibits meet design, budget, and schedule requirements.","core":false,"importance":3.77,"relevance":65,"frequency":2.92},{"id":9291,"text":"Inspect installed exhibits for conformance to specifications and satisfactory operation of special-effects components.","core":true,"importance":3.76,"relevance":90.48,"frequency":2.63},{"id":9288,"text":"Estimate set- or exhibit-related costs, including materials, construction, and rental of props or locations.","core":true,"importance":3.67,"relevance":80,"frequency":2.69},{"id":9310,"text":"Coordinate the transportation of sets that are built off-site, and coordinate their setup at the site of use.","core":false,"importance":3.67,"relevance":57.14,"frequency":2.33},{"id":9301,"text":"Confer with conservators to determine how to handle an exhibit's environmental aspects, such as lighting, temperature, and humidity, so that objects will be protected and exhibits will be enhanced.","core":false,"importance":3.58,"relevance":60,"frequency":2.18},{"id":9292,"text":"Plan for location-specific issues, such as space limitations, traffic flow patterns, and safety concerns.","core":true,"importance":3.56,"relevance":85.71,"frequency":2.44},{"id":9295,"text":"Select and purchase lumber and hardware necessary for set construction.","core":false,"importance":3.5,"relevance":50,"frequency":2.44},{"id":9285,"text":"Acquire, or arrange for acquisition of, specimens or graphics required to complete exhibits.","core":true,"importance":3.44,"relevance":85.71,"frequency":2.44},{"id":9307,"text":"Arrange for outside contractors to construct exhibit structures.","core":false,"importance":3.36,"relevance":57.14,"frequency":2.5},{"id":9298,"text":"Design and produce displays and materials that can be used to decorate windows, interior displays, or event locations, such as streets and fairgrounds.","core":true,"importance":3,"relevance":75,"frequency":2},{"id":9309,"text":"Incorporate security systems into exhibit layouts.","core":false,"importance":3,"relevance":35,"frequency":1.86},{"id":9299,"text":"Coordinate the removal of sets, props, and exhibits after productions or events are complete.","core":false,"importance":2.83,"relevance":60,"frequency":1.92},{"id":9308,"text":"Provide supportive materials for exhibits and displays, such as press kits, advertising, publicity notices, posters, brochures, catalogues, and invitations.","core":false,"importance":2.62,"relevance":38.1,"frequency":2.25}],"activities":[{"id":"4.A.2.b.2","importan